  "terms": {
    "en": "Prohibition and advice",
    "es": "Prohibición y consejo",
    "it": "Divieto e consiglio",
    "fr": "Interdiction et conseil",
    "de": "Verbot und Rat",
    "ru": "Запрет и совет",
    "hu": "Tilalom és tanács",
    "pt": "Proibição e conselho",
    "ro": "Interdicție și sfat"
  },
  "locales": {
    "en": {
      "title": "Prohibition and advice",
      "summary": "Mustn't forbids; shouldn't advises against.",
      "status": "draft",
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "What it is",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraphs",
              "paragraphs": [
                "Modal verbs can say that something is forbidden or that it is a bad idea. The strength changes with the verb: some forms forbid, others only advise."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "You **mustn't** smoke here. (forbidden)",
                "You **can't** park there. (not allowed)",
                "You **shouldn't** eat so much sugar. (a bad idea)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "How it works in English",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "table",
              "html": "<table><thead><tr><th>Form</th><th>Strength</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>must not (mustn't)</strong></td><td>a strong prohibition</td><td><strong>You mustn't touch it.</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>can't / may not</strong></td><td>a rule or law</td><td><strong>You can't smoke inside.</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>not allowed to</strong></td><td>a rule</td><td><strong>Visitors aren't allowed to enter.</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>shouldn't / ought not to</strong></td><td>advice against</td><td><strong>You shouldn't stay up late.</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>had better not</strong></td><td>strong warning</td><td><strong>You'd better not be late.</strong></td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Advice for and against",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "table",
              "html": "<table><thead><tr><th>For</th><th>Against</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>You should see a doctor.</strong></td><td><strong>You shouldn't ignore it.</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>You ought to apologise.</strong></td><td><strong>You ought not to shout.</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>You'd better take an umbrella.</strong></td><td><strong>You'd better not go out.</strong></td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Giving a reason",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraphs",
              "paragraphs": [
                "Prohibitions often come with a reason beginning with because or otherwise: You mustn't park here, because it is a bus stop. Take your umbrella, otherwise you'll get wet."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Common mistakes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Wrong: **You mustn't to go.** Right: **You mustn't go.**",
                "Wrong: **You don't must smoke.** Right: **You mustn't smoke.**",
                "Wrong: **He shouldn't to speak.** Right: **He shouldn't speak.**",
                "Do not confuse **mustn't** (forbidden) with **needn't** (not necessary)."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
